  "verbalization": "Ardisiamamilloside F appears to exert its biological effects through a shared target, Protein kinase C eta, which is implicated in multiple downstream pathways leading to Jurkat cell activation. This relationship is supported by the presence of a direct interaction between Ardisiamamilloside F and Protein kinase C eta, with this kinase being a target of several compounds, including Cyclopent-2-Enone, Oleodaphnone, and Lythrine, all of which also target Jurkat. The consistent scores across the three paths suggest a robust, albeit indirect, connection between Ardisiamamilloside F and Jurkat, likely through the intermediate step of Protein kinase C eta. The mechanism appears to involve the activation of Jurkat cells via the modulation of this kinase, which may be a common pathway among the compounds in the dataset. The integration of these findings highlights the potential for Ardisiamamilloside F to act through a similar mechanism, emphasizing the role of Protein kinase C eta in mediating its effects on Jurkat.",
